concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-577 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "577 Simplified outline"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-577 ;
    values:originalText "The following is a simplified outline of this Part: • Telstra may give the following undertakings:  (a) an undertaking about structural separation;  (b) an undertaking about hybrid fibre-coaxial networks;  (c) an undertaking about subscription television broadcasting licences. • An undertaking comes into force when it is accepted by the ACCC. • The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that the excluded spectrum regime applies to Telstra. If the Minister does so, Telstra will not be allowed to supply services using a designated part of the spectrum unless all 3 undertakings given by Telstra are in force. • However, the Minister may exempt Telstra from the requirement to have an undertaking about hybrid fibre-coaxial networks or subscription television broadcasting licences if the Minister is satisfied that Telstra’s undertaking about structural separation is sufficient to address concerns about the degree of Telstra’s power in telecommunications markets. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00891  Amendments  Schedule 1 Amendments relating to Telstra  Part 1  Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer Safeguards) Act 2010          11" ;
    skos:definition "The following is a simplified outline of this Part: • Telstra may give the following undertakings:  (a) an undertaking about structural separation;  (b) an undertaking about hybrid fibre-coaxial networks;  (c) an undertaking about subscription television broadcasting licences. • An undertaking comes into force when it is accepted by the ACCC. • The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that the excluded spectrum regime applies to Telstra. If the Minister does so, Telstra will not be allowed to supply services using a designated part of the spectrum unless all 3 undertakings given by Telstra are in force. • However, the Minister may exempt Telstra from the requirement to have an undertaking about hybrid fibre-coaxial networks or subscription television broadcasting licences if the Minister is satisfied that Telstra’s undertaking about structural separation is sufficient to address concerns about the degree of Telstra’s power in telecommunications markets. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00891  Amendments  Schedule 1 Amendments relating to Telstra  Part 1  Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer Safeguards) Act 2010          11"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "9bc7eb458e380939d016238d5e1eb753231f6e752b6d2bad79b4b9acefa5b271" ;
    cof:pageNumber "14"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Telstra undertakes about structural separation, hybrid fibre-coaxial networks, and subscription television broadcasting licences." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010.pdf, p.14" ;
    cml:asserts concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-577-norm .
