doc:sch-1-sec-18-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "18 Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "Consumer Safeguards) Act 2010 577AB  When undertaking about structural separation comes into force  An undertaking under section 577A comes into force:  (a) if:  (i) the decision to accept the undertaking is expressed to be subject to the occurrence of a single specified event within a specified period; and  (ii) the event occurs within that period;  when the event occurs; or  (b) if:  (i) the decision to accept the undertaking is expressed to be subject to the occurrence of 2 or more specified events within a specified period; and  (ii) each of those events occur at the same time; and  (iii) that time occurs within that period;  at that time; or  (c) if:  (i) the decision to accept the undertaking is expressed to be subject to the occurrence of 2 or more specified events within a specified period; and  (ii) each of those events occur at different times; and  (iii) each of those times occur within that period;  at the last of those times; or  (d) if the decision to accept the undertaking is not expressed to be subject to the occurrence of one or more specified events within a specified period—when the undertaking is accepted by the ACCC." ;
    cof:pageNumber "22"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-577ac a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "577AC Publication requirements for undertaking about structural"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-577ac ;
    values:originalText "separation  (1) If a decision to accept an undertaking under section 577A is expressed to be subject to the occurrence of one or more specified events within a specified period, the ACCC must:  (a) as soon as practicable after making the decision, publish on its website:  (i) the undertaking; and  (ii) the terms of the decision; and ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00891  Amendments  Schedule 1 Amendments relating to Telstra  Part 1  Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer Safeguards) Act 2010          19  (b) as soon as practicable after the ACCC becomes aware that the undertaking has come into force, publish on its website a notice announcing that the undertaking has come into force.  (2) If a decision to accept an undertaking under section 577A is not expressed to be subject to the occurrence of one or more specified events within a specified period, the ACCC must, as soon as practicable after accepting the undertaking, publish the undertaking on its website." ;
    skos:definition "separation  (1) If a decision to accept an undertaking under section 577A is expressed to be subject to the occurrence of one or more specified events within a specified period, the ACCC must:  (a) as soon as practicable after making the decision, publish on its website:  (i) the undertaking; and  (ii) the terms of the decision; and ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00891  Amendments  Schedule 1 Amendments relating to Telstra  Part 1  Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer Safeguards) Act 2010          19  (b) as soon as practicable after the ACCC becomes aware that the undertaking has come into force, publish on its website a notice announcing that the undertaking has come into force.  (2) If a decision to accept an undertaking under section 577A is not expressed to be subject to the occurrence of one or more specified events within a specified period, the ACCC must, as soon as practicable after accepting the undertaking, publish the undertaking on its website."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "66af36d5b0569fdef4d95c9009848f15ee8fe9268d36fd5ea4f8493f12e0d707" ;
    cof:pageNumber "22"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-577ac-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-577ac-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
