    skos:definition "(1) The object of this section is to promote the national interest in structural reform of the telecommunications industry by authorising, for the purposes of subsection 51(1) of the Competition and Consumer Act 2010, certain conduct engaged in by:  (a) Telstra; and  (b) NBN corporations; and  (c) certain other persons. Note: If conduct is authorised for the purposes of subsection 51(1) of the Competition and Consumer Act 2010, the conduct is disregarded in deciding whether a person has contravened Part IV of that Act. Authorised conduct"@en ;
