concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-577bc a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "577BC Migration plan"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-577bc ;
    values:originalText "(1) The specified action first mentioned in paragraph 577A(1)(b) may include giving the ACCC a draft migration plan after the relevant undertaking has come into force.  (2) A draft or final migration plan must:  (a) specify the action to be taken by Telstra to:  (i) cease to supply fixed-line carriage services to customers using a telecommunications network over which Telstra is in a position to exercise control; and ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00891  Schedule 1  Amendments" ;
    skos:definition "(1) The specified action first mentioned in paragraph 577A(1)(b) may include giving the ACCC a draft migration plan after the relevant undertaking has come into force.  (2) A draft or final migration plan must:  (a) specify the action to be taken by Telstra to:  (i) cease to supply fixed-line carriage services to customers using a telecommunications network over which Telstra is in a position to exercise control; and ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00891  Schedule 1  Amendments"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "9deffa070631e83e3667804f08eb8948b4882dc9ddb97caef798942ad8f9b4e1" ;
