doc:sch-1-sec-30-2-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "30(1) Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) If:  (a) Telstra gives the ACCC an undertaking under section 577A; and ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00891  Amendments  Schedule 1 Amendments relating to Telstra  Part 1  Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer Safeguards) Act 2010          31  (b) the specified action first mentioned in paragraph 577A(1)(b) consists of, or includes, giving the ACCC a draft migration plan after the undertaking has come into force; and  (c) the following conditions are satisfied:  (i) Telstra has, in a document accompanying the undertaking, nominated the event mentioned in subparagraph 577AA(1)(c)(vi);  (ii) the nomination meets the requirements of paragraph 577AA(1)(b) and subsection 577AA(2); Telstra may give the ACCC a draft migration plan (the original plan) during the period:  (d) beginning when Telstra gives the ACCC the undertaking; and  (e) ending when the undertaking comes into force; as if the undertaking had come into force. Decision" ;
    cof:pageNumber "34"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-30-2-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "30(2) Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-30-2-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) The ACCC must:  (a) if the ACCC is satisfied that the original plan complies with the migration plan principles—approve the original plan; or  (b) otherwise:  (i) refuse to approve the original plan; and  (ii) by written notice given to Telstra, request Telstra to give the ACCC, within 30 days after the notice is given, a replacement draft migration plan that complies with the migration plan principles. Note 1: For migration plan principles, see section 577BB. Note 2: If Telstra gives the ACCC a replacement draft migration plan in response to the request, the ACCC will make a decision about the plan under section 577BDC." ;
    skos:definition "(2) The ACCC must:  (a) if the ACCC is satisfied that the original plan complies with the migration plan principles—approve the original plan; or  (b) otherwise:  (i) refuse to approve the original plan; and  (ii) by written notice given to Telstra, request Telstra to give the ACCC, within 30 days after the notice is given, a replacement draft migration plan that complies with the migration plan principles. Note 1: For migration plan principles, see section 577BB. Note 2: If Telstra gives the ACCC a replacement draft migration plan in response to the request, the ACCC will make a decision about the plan under section 577BDC."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "aaade8fe456d8745cdf03506cae0c6ac977a25b87ffb4e48c79d730a79ed4ac2" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-30-2 ;
    cof:pageNumber "34"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Request for Telstra to provide a replacement draft migration plan within 30 days." ;
    dc:description "Replacement draft migration plan" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
