doc:sch-1-sec-34-ss-5 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "34(5) Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(5) As soon as practicable after making a decision under subsection (2), the ACCC must notify Telstra in writing of the decision." ;
    cof:pageNumber "38"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-577be a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "577BE Effect of approval of draft migration plan"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-577be ;
    values:originalText "(1) If the ACCC approves a draft migration plan, the plan becomes a final migration plan.  (2) If the ACCC approves a draft migration plan under subsection 577BD(2), the plan comes into force at the start of the day after notice of the decision to approve the plan is given to Telstra in accordance with subsection 577BD(6).  (3) If the ACCC approves a draft migration plan under subsection 577BDA(2), 577BDB(2) or 577BDC(2), the plan comes into force at the later of:  (a) the start of the day after notice of the decision to approve the plan is given to Telstra in accordance with subsection 577BDA(7), 577BDB(6) or 577BDC(5), as the case requires; or  (b) when the relevant undertaking under section 577A comes into force. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00891  Schedule 1  Amendments" ;
    skos:definition "(1) If the ACCC approves a draft migration plan, the plan becomes a final migration plan.  (2) If the ACCC approves a draft migration plan under subsection 577BD(2), the plan comes into force at the start of the day after notice of the decision to approve the plan is given to Telstra in accordance with subsection 577BD(6).  (3) If the ACCC approves a draft migration plan under subsection 577BDA(2), 577BDB(2) or 577BDC(2), the plan comes into force at the later of:  (a) the start of the day after notice of the decision to approve the plan is given to Telstra in accordance with subsection 577BDA(7), 577BDB(6) or 577BDC(5), as the case requires; or  (b) when the relevant undertaking under section 577A comes into force. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00891  Schedule 1  Amendments"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "00e6dea749fd211fda88ff970ba1786c373cc4e1ec273deac86081b3d0b633ba" ;
    cof:pageNumber "39"^^xsd:integer ;
