doc:sch-1-sec-52-ss-6 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "52(6) Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(6) The Minister must not make a declaration under subsection (5) unless the ACCC has made a decision to accept an undertaking given by Telstra under section 577A, and:  (a) if the undertaking is in force—the Minister is satisfied that the undertaking is sufficient to address concerns about the degree of Telstra’s power in telecommunications markets; or  (b) if the undertaking is not in force—the Minister is satisfied that, subject to the undertaking coming into force, the undertaking is sufficient to address concerns about the degree of Telstra’s power in telecommunications markets." ;
    cof:pageNumber "56"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-52-ss-6a a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "52(6A) Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-52-ss-6a ;
    values:originalText "(6A) A declaration under subsection (5) comes into force:  (a) if paragraph (6)(a) applies—when the declaration is made; or ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00891  Amendments  Schedule 1 Amendments relating to Telstra  Part 1  Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer Safeguards) Act 2010          53  (b) if paragraph (6)(b) applies—when the undertaking comes into force." ;
    skos:definition "(6A) A declaration under subsection (5) comes into force:  (a) if paragraph (6)(a) applies—when the declaration is made; or ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00891  Amendments  Schedule 1 Amendments relating to Telstra  Part 1  Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer Safeguards) Act 2010          53  (b) if paragraph (6)(b) applies—when the undertaking comes into force."@en ;
