doc:sch-1-sec-577k-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "577K(2) Limits on use of certain spectrum licences by Telstra" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) However, the rule in subsection (1) does not apply if:  (a) both:  (i) an undertaking given by Telstra is in force under section 577A; and  (ii) the undertaking is covered by subsection (2A); and  (b) either:  (i) an undertaking given by Telstra is in force under section 577C; or  (ii) a declaration is in force under subsection 577J(3); and ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00891  Schedule 1  Amendments" ;
    cof:pageNumber "57"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-54 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "54 Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-54 ;
    values:originalText "Consumer Safeguards) Act 2010  (c) either:  (i) an undertaking given by Telstra is in force under section 577E; or  (ii) a declaration is in force under subsection 577J(5). Note 1: Section 577A deals with undertakings about structural separation. Note 2: Section 577C deals with undertakings about hybrid fibre-coaxial networks. Note 3: Section 577E deals with undertakings about subscription television broadcasting licences.  (2A) This subsection covers a section 577A undertaking if:  (a) the following conditions are satisfied:  (i) the undertaking requires Telstra to give the ACCC a draft migration plan;  (ii) in accordance with the undertaking, Telstra has given the ACCC a draft migration plan;  (iii) the ACCC has approved the draft migration plan under section 577BD, 577BDA, 577BDB or 577BDC; or  (b) the undertaking does not require Telstra to give the ACCC a draft migration plan.  (3) A person must not:  (a) aid, abet, counsel or procure a contravention of subsection (1); or  (b) induce, whether by threats or promises or otherwise, a contravention of subsection (1); or  (c) be in any way, directly or indirectly, knowingly concerned in, or party to, a contravention of subsection (1); or  (d) conspire with others to effect a contravention of subsection (1).  (4) Subsections (1) and (3) are civil penalty provisions. Note: Part 31 provides for pecuniary penalties for breaches of civil penalty provisions." ;
    skos:definition "Consumer Safeguards) Act 2010  (c) either:  (i) an undertaking given by Telstra is in force under section 577E; or  (ii) a declaration is in force under subsection 577J(5). Note 1: Section 577A deals with undertakings about structural separation. Note 2: Section 577C deals with undertakings about hybrid fibre-coaxial networks. Note 3: Section 577E deals with undertakings about subscription television broadcasting licences.  (2A) This subsection covers a section 577A undertaking if:  (a) the following conditions are satisfied:  (i) the undertaking requires Telstra to give the ACCC a draft migration plan;  (ii) in accordance with the undertaking, Telstra has given the ACCC a draft migration plan;  (iii) the ACCC has approved the draft migration plan under section 577BD, 577BDA, 577BDB or 577BDC; or  (b) the undertaking does not require Telstra to give the ACCC a draft migration plan.  (3) A person must not:  (a) aid, abet, counsel or procure a contravention of subsection (1); or  (b) induce, whether by threats or promises or otherwise, a contravention of subsection (1); or  (c) be in any way, directly or indirectly, knowingly concerned in, or party to, a contravention of subsection (1); or  (d) conspire with others to effect a contravention of subsection (1).  (4) Subsections (1) and (3) are civil penalty provisions. Note: Part 31 provides for pecuniary penalties for breaches of civil penalty provisions."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "00f1868399864678ac1a887647407ce0555b02be60cb376fa32f8aa9f2baeaa0" ;
    cof:pageNumber "58"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-54-ss-2a ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-54-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-54-ss-4 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010.pdf, p.58" .
doc:sch-1-sec-54 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "54 Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "Consumer Safeguards) Act 2010  (c) either:  (i) an undertaking given by Telstra is in force under section 577E; or  (ii) a declaration is in force under subsection 577J(5). Note 1: Section 577A deals with undertakings about structural separation. Note 2: Section 577C deals with undertakings about hybrid fibre-coaxial networks. Note 3: Section 577E deals with undertakings about subscription television broadcasting licences.  (2A) This subsection covers a section 577A undertaking if:  (a) the following conditions are satisfied:  (i) the undertaking requires Telstra to give the ACCC a draft migration plan;  (ii) in accordance with the undertaking, Telstra has given the ACCC a draft migration plan;  (iii) the ACCC has approved the draft migration plan under section 577BD, 577BDA, 577BDB or 577BDC; or  (b) the undertaking does not require Telstra to give the ACCC a draft migration plan.  (3) A person must not:  (a) aid, abet, counsel or procure a contravention of subsection (1); or  (b) induce, whether by threats or promises or otherwise, a contravention of subsection (1); or  (c) be in any way, directly or indirectly, knowingly concerned in, or party to, a contravention of subsection (1); or  (d) conspire with others to effect a contravention of subsection (1).  (4) Subsections (1) and (3) are civil penalty provisions. Note: Part 31 provides for pecuniary penalties for breaches of civil penalty provisions." ;
    cof:pageNumber "58"^^xsd:integer .

