concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-577l-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "577L(2) Limits on assignment of certain spectrum licences to Telstra"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-577l-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) However, the rule in subsection (1) does not apply if:  (a) both:  (i) an undertaking given by Telstra is in force under section 577A; and  (ii) the undertaking is covered by subsection (2A); and  (b) either:  (i) an undertaking given by Telstra is in force under section 577C; or  (ii) a declaration is in force under subsection 577J(3); and  (c) either:  (i) an undertaking given by Telstra is in force under section 577E; or  (ii) a declaration is in force under subsection 577J(5). Note 1: Section 577A deals with undertakings about structural separation. Note 2: Section 577C deals with undertakings about hybrid fibre-coaxial networks. Note 3: Section 577E deals with undertakings about subscription television broadcasting licences." ;
    skos:definition "(2) However, the rule in subsection (1) does not apply if:  (a) both:  (i) an undertaking given by Telstra is in force under section 577A; and  (ii) the undertaking is covered by subsection (2A); and  (b) either:  (i) an undertaking given by Telstra is in force under section 577C; or  (ii) a declaration is in force under subsection 577J(3); and  (c) either:  (i) an undertaking given by Telstra is in force under section 577E; or  (ii) a declaration is in force under subsection 577J(5). Note 1: Section 577A deals with undertakings about structural separation. Note 2: Section 577C deals with undertakings about hybrid fibre-coaxial networks. Note 3: Section 577E deals with undertakings about subscription television broadcasting licences."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "c0cf94b0515a980c2033c1228a9628d5225072c7e41b6e9c4700d134dcbca0ce" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-577l ;
