doc:sch-1-sec-70 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "70 Declared network services" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "For the purposes of this Part, a declared network service is a service specified in a legislative instrument made by the Minister for the purposes of this clause. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00891  Amendments  Schedule 1 Amendments relating to Telstra  Part 1  Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer Safeguards) Act 2010          61" ;
    cof:pageNumber "64"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-71 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "71 Regulated services"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-71 ;
    values:originalText "(1) For the purposes of this Part, a regulated service is a declared service within the meaning of Part XIC of the Competition and Consumer Act 2010.  (2) Subclause (1) has effect subject to subclause (3).  (3) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that a specified service is not a regulated service for the purposes of this Part.  (4) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that a specified eligible service is a regulated service for the purposes of this Part." ;
    skos:definition "(1) For the purposes of this Part, a regulated service is a declared service within the meaning of Part XIC of the Competition and Consumer Act 2010.  (2) Subclause (1) has effect subject to subclause (3).  (3) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that a specified service is not a regulated service for the purposes of this Part.  (4) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that a specified eligible service is a regulated service for the purposes of this Part."@en ;
