    cof:title "64(5A) Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(5A) Subclause (5) does not apply if, before the end of the period applicable under subclause (5):  (a) the following conditions are satisfied:  (i) an undertaking given by Telstra is in force under section 577A;  (ii) the undertaking requires Telstra to give the ACCC a draft migration plan;  (iii) in accordance with the undertaking, Telstra has given the ACCC a draft migration plan; ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00891  Amendments  Schedule 1 Amendments relating to Telstra  Part 1  Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer Safeguards) Act 2010          65  (iv) the ACCC has approved the draft migration plan under section 577BD, 577BDA, 577BDB or 577BDC; or  (b) both:  (i) an undertaking given by Telstra is in force under section 577A; and  (ii) the undertaking does not require Telstra to give the ACCC a draft migration plan. Note: Section 577A deals with undertakings about structural separation." ;
    cof:pageNumber "68"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-64-ss-5b a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "64(5B) Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-64-ss-5b ;
    values:originalText "(5B) The Minister may, by writing, extend or further extend the 90-day period referred to in subclause (5) so long as the extension, or the total of the extensions, does not exceed 18 months." ;
    skos:definition "(5B) The Minister may, by writing, extend or further extend the 90-day period referred to in subclause (5) so long as the extension, or the total of the extensions, does not exceed 18 months."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "1a3cbc519952ce853af5a868cc417836ab8c3ffba9048cefd38268f991fe5630" ;
