concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-70-2-ss-7 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "70(7) Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-70-2-ss-7 ;
    values:originalText "(7) The Minister does not have a duty to consider whether to exercise the power to make a subclause (3) instrument, whether he or she is requested to do so by Telstra or by any other person, or in any other circumstances." ;
    skos:definition "(7) The Minister does not have a duty to consider whether to exercise the power to make a subclause (3) instrument, whether he or she is requested to do so by Telstra or by any other person, or in any other circumstances."@en ;
