concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-77 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "77 Approval of draft functional separation undertaking by Minister"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-77 ;
    values:originalText "(1) This clause applies if Telstra gives the Minister a draft functional separation undertaking (the original undertaking).  (2) The Minister must, by writing:  (a) approve the original undertaking; or ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00891  Amendments  Schedule 1 Amendments relating to Telstra  Part 1  Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer Safeguards) Act 2010          71  (b) both:  (i) vary the original undertaking; and  (ii) approve the original undertaking as varied; or  (c) both:  (i) determine that Telstra is taken to have given the Minister another draft functional separation undertaking (the replacement undertaking) in the terms specified in the determination, instead of the original undertaking; and  (ii) approve the replacement undertaking. Consultation  (3) Before making a decision under subclause (2), the Minister must:  (a) cause to be published on the Department’s website a notice:  (i) setting out the original undertaking; and  (ii) inviting persons to make submissions to the Minister about the original undertaking within 14 days after the notice is published; and  (b) give the ACCC a copy of the notice; and  (c) cause to be published on the Department’s website a copy of each submission received within the 14-day period mentioned in paragraph (a); and  (d) consider any submissions received within the 14-day period mentioned in paragraph (a); and  (e) ask the ACCC to give advice to the Minister, within 44 days after the notice is published, about the original undertaking; and  (f) have regard to any advice given by the ACCC. Consultation—variation of original undertaking  (4) Before making a decision under paragraph (2)(b) to approve the original undertaking as varied, the Minister must:  (a) give Telstra a notice:  (i) setting out the original undertaking as proposed to be varied; and  (ii) inviting Telstra to make submissions to the Minister, within 14 days after the notice is given, about the original undertaking as proposed to be varied; and ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00891  Schedule 1  Amendments" ;
    skos:definition "(1) This clause applies if Telstra gives the Minister a draft functional separation undertaking (the original undertaking).  (2) The Minister must, by writing:  (a) approve the original undertaking; or ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00891  Amendments  Schedule 1 Amendments relating to Telstra  Part 1  Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer Safeguards) Act 2010          71  (b) both:  (i) vary the original undertaking; and  (ii) approve the original undertaking as varied; or  (c) both:  (i) determine that Telstra is taken to have given the Minister another draft functional separation undertaking (the replacement undertaking) in the terms specified in the determination, instead of the original undertaking; and  (ii) approve the replacement undertaking. Consultation  (3) Before making a decision under subclause (2), the Minister must:  (a) cause to be published on the Department’s website a notice:  (i) setting out the original undertaking; and  (ii) inviting persons to make submissions to the Minister about the original undertaking within 14 days after the notice is published; and  (b) give the ACCC a copy of the notice; and  (c) cause to be published on the Department’s website a copy of each submission received within the 14-day period mentioned in paragraph (a); and  (d) consider any submissions received within the 14-day period mentioned in paragraph (a); and  (e) ask the ACCC to give advice to the Minister, within 44 days after the notice is published, about the original undertaking; and  (f) have regard to any advice given by the ACCC. Consultation—variation of original undertaking  (4) Before making a decision under paragraph (2)(b) to approve the original undertaking as varied, the Minister must:  (a) give Telstra a notice:  (i) setting out the original undertaking as proposed to be varied; and  (ii) inviting Telstra to make submissions to the Minister, within 14 days after the notice is given, about the original undertaking as prop"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "3d28f75fdaee1cd3de622ed0525d54a4446acb2d3e7790eebb72abccb84c5dfe" ;
    cof:pageNumber "74"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-77-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-77-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-77-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-77-ss-4 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010.pdf, p.74" .
doc:sch-1-sec-77 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "77 Approval of draft functional separation undertaking by Minister" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) This clause applies if Telstra gives the Minister a draft functional separation undertaking (the original undertaking).  (2) The Minister must, by writing:  (a) approve the original undertaking; or ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00891  Amendments  Schedule 1 Amendments relating to Telstra  Part 1  Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer Safeguards) Act 2010          71  (b) both:  (i) vary the original undertaking; and  (ii) approve the original undertaking as varied; or  (c) both:  (i) determine that Telstra is taken to have given the Minister another draft functional separation undertaking (the replacement undertaking) in the terms specified in the determination, instead of the original undertaking; and  (ii) approve the replacement undertaking. Consultation  (3) Before making a decision under subclause (2), the Minister must:  (a) cause to be published on the Department’s website a notice:  (i) setting out the original undertaking; and  (ii) inviting persons to make submissions to the Minister about the original undertaking within 14 days after the notice is published; and  (b) give the ACCC a copy of the notice; and  (c) cause to be published on the Department’s website a copy of each submission received within the 14-day period mentioned in paragraph (a); and  (d) consider any submissions received within the 14-day period mentioned in paragraph (a); and  (e) ask the ACCC to give advice to the Minister, within 44 days after the notice is published, about the original undertaking; and  (f) have regard to any advice given by the ACCC. Consultation—variation of original undertaking  (4) Before making a decision under paragraph (2)(b) to approve the original undertaking as varied, the Minister must:  (a) give Telstra a notice:  (i) setting out the original undertaking as proposed to be varied; and  (ii) inviting Telstra to make submissions to the Minister, within 14 days after the notice is given, about the original undertaking as proposed to be varied; and ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00891  Schedule 1  Amendments" ;
    cof:pageNumber "74"^^xsd:integer .

