doc:sch-1-sec-77-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "77(2) Approval of draft functional separation undertaking by Minister" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) The Minister must, by writing:  (a) approve the original undertaking; or ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00891  Amendments  Schedule 1 Amendments relating to Telstra  Part 1  Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer Safeguards) Act 2010          71  (b) both:  (i) vary the original undertaking; and  (ii) approve the original undertaking as varied; or  (c) both:  (i) determine that Telstra is taken to have given the Minister another draft functional separation undertaking (the replacement undertaking) in the terms specified in the determination, instead of the original undertaking; and  (ii) approve the replacement undertaking. Consultation" ;
    cof:pageNumber "74"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-77-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "77(3) Approval of draft functional separation undertaking by Minister"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-77-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) Before making a decision under subclause (2), the Minister must:  (a) cause to be published on the Department’s website a notice:  (i) setting out the original undertaking; and  (ii) inviting persons to make submissions to the Minister about the original undertaking within 14 days after the notice is published; and  (b) give the ACCC a copy of the notice; and  (c) cause to be published on the Department’s website a copy of each submission received within the 14-day period mentioned in paragraph (a); and  (d) consider any submissions received within the 14-day period mentioned in paragraph (a); and  (e) ask the ACCC to give advice to the Minister, within 44 days after the notice is published, about the original undertaking; and  (f) have regard to any advice given by the ACCC. Consultation—variation of original undertaking" ;
    skos:definition "(3) Before making a decision under subclause (2), the Minister must:  (a) cause to be published on the Department’s website a notice:  (i) setting out the original undertaking; and  (ii) inviting persons to make submissions to the Minister about the original undertaking within 14 days after the notice is published; and  (b) give the ACCC a copy of the notice; and  (c) cause to be published on the Department’s website a copy of each submission received within the 14-day period mentioned in paragraph (a); and  (d) consider any submissions received within the 14-day period mentioned in paragraph (a); and  (e) ask the ACCC to give advice to the Minister, within 44 days after the notice is published, about the original undertaking; and  (f) have regard to any advice given by the ACCC. Consultation—variation of original undertaking"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "e2da6ef1b835022113d17cd54493f5bc1f996851a1c9d355bbeb7f9cdf0047c8" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-77 ;
    cof:pageNumber "74"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Minister must consult with ACCC before making a decision on the original undertaking." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
