    cof:pageNumber "82"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-86 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "86 Associate"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-86 ;
    values:originalText "(1) In this Part, an associate of Telstra in relation to control of a spectrum licence is:  (a) a partner of Telstra; or ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00891  Amendments  Schedule 1 Amendments relating to Telstra  Part 1  Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer Safeguards) Act 2010          79  (b) if Telstra or another person who is an associate of Telstra under another paragraph receives benefits or is capable of benefiting under a trust—the trustee of the trust; or  (c) a person (whether a company or not) who:  (i) acts, or is accustomed to act; or  (ii) under a contract or an arrangement or understanding (whether formal or informal) is intended or expected to act;  in accordance with the directions, instructions or wishes of, or in concert with:  (iii) Telstra; or  (iv) Telstra and another person who is an associate of Telstra under another paragraph; or  (d) another company if:  (i) the other company is a related body corporate of Telstra for the purposes of the Corporations Act 2001; or  (ii) Telstra, or Telstra and another person who is an associate of Telstra under another paragraph, are in a position to exercise control of the other company.  (2) However, persons are not associates of each other if the ACCC is satisfied that:  (a) they do not act together in any relevant dealings relating to the spectrum licence; and  (b) neither of them is in a position to exert influence over the business dealings of the other in relation to the spectrum licence." ;
    skos:definition "(1) In this Part, an associate of Telstra in relation to control of a spectrum licence is:  (a) a partner of Telstra; or ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00891  Amendments  Schedule 1 Amendments relating to Telstra  Part 1  Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer Safeguards) Act 2010          79  (b) if Telstra or another person who is an associate of Telstra under another paragraph receives benefits or is capable of benefiting under a trust—the trustee of the trust; or  (c) a person (whether a company or not) who:  (i) acts, or is accustomed to act; or  (ii) under a contract or an arrangement or understanding (whether formal or informal) is intended or expected to act;  in accordance with the directions, instructions or wishes of, or in concert with:  (iii) Telstra; or  (iv) Telstra and another person who is an associate of Telstra under another paragraph; or  (d) another company if:  (i) the other company is a related body corporate of Telstra for the purposes of the Corporations Act 2001; or  (ii) Telstra, or Telstra and another person who is an associate of Telstra under another paragraph, are in a position to exercise control of the other company.  (2) However, persons are not associates of each other if the ACCC is satisfied that:  (a) they do not act together in any relevant dealings relating to the spectrum licence; and  (b) neither of them is in a position to exert influence over the business dealings of the other in relation to the spectrum licence."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "604cc14b29ee729aac3c8b2e183225b5cf1952923f1e32abc7c403f9117b698d" ;
    cof:pageNumber "82"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-86-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-86-ss-2 ;
