concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-50-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "50 Section 104"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-50-2 ;
    values:originalText "After: • The ACMA may be directed by the Minister to monitor, and report on, specified matters relating to the performance of carriers and carriage service providers. insert: • The ACCC is to monitor, and report each year to the Minister on, the compliance by Telstra with a final functional separation undertaking. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00891  Amendments  Schedule 1 Amendments relating to Telstra  Part 1  Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer Safeguards) Act 2010          85" ;
    skos:definition "After: • The ACMA may be directed by the Minister to monitor, and report on, specified matters relating to the performance of carriers and carriage service providers. insert: • The ACCC is to monitor, and report each year to the Minister on, the compliance by Telstra with a final functional separation undertaking. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00891  Amendments  Schedule 1 Amendments relating to Telstra  Part 1  Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer Safeguards) Act 2010          85"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "4b833e2728885b4ca975da43771ad500543ee42a988727a3ead00ca0b768c507" ;
    cof:pageNumber "88"^^xsd:integer ;
