doc:sch-1-sec-100-ss-2b a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "100(2B) Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2B) If, at the time the request was made:  (a) one or more provisions (the contingent provisions) of a contract have not come into force because:  (i) the contingent provisions are subject to a condition precedent; and  (ii) the condition precedent has not been satisfied; and  (b) there is a possibility that the condition precedent could become satisfied; and  (c) assuming that the condition precedent had been satisfied:  (i) the contingent provisions would come into force; and  (ii) the person would have a right under the contingent provisions; paragraph (2A)(a) has effect, in relation to the contract, as if, at the time the request was made:  (d) the contract was in force; and  (e) the person had the right under the contract." ;
    cof:pageNumber "104"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-94-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "94 After subclause 17(4) of Schedule 1"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-94-2 ;
    values:originalText "Insert:  (4A) For the purposes of subclause (1), if:  (a) there is an agreement in force between Telstra and an NBN corporation; and  (b) the agreement relates to the NBN corporation’s access to facilities owned or operated by Telstra; and  (c) apart from this clause, the agreement would result in the NBN corporation being the operator of the facilities; ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00891  Amendments  Schedule 1 Telecommunications access regime  Part 2  Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer Safeguards) Act 2010          101 the NBN corporation is taken not to be the operator of the facilities." ;
    skos:definition "Insert:  (4A) For the purposes of subclause (1), if:  (a) there is an agreement in force between Telstra and an NBN corporation; and  (b) the agreement relates to the NBN corporation’s access to facilities owned or operated by Telstra; and  (c) apart from this clause, the agreement would result in the NBN corporation being the operator of the facilities; ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00891  Amendments  Schedule 1 Telecommunications access regime  Part 2  Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer Safeguards) Act 2010          101 the NBN corporation is taken not to be the operator of the facilities."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "4dc8383adcbf2fedb0e7131f81ada6279f0e61d02ab81c85d5f9e7541c51036a" ;
    cof:pageNumber "104"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "NBN corporation is not the operator of facilities if agreement with Telstra would result in that." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010.pdf> ;
