concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-118-2-ss-1 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "118(1) Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-118-2-ss-1 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Commission must take the following matters into account in making an access determination:  (a) whether the determination will promote the long-term interests of end-users of carriage services or of services supplied by means of carriage services;  (b) the legitimate business interests of a carrier or carriage service provider who supplies, or is capable of supplying, the declared service, and the carrier’s or provider’s investment in facilities used to supply the declared service;  (c) the interests of all persons who have rights to use the declared service;  (d) the direct costs of providing access to the declared service;  (e) the value to a person of extensions, or enhancement of capability, whose cost is borne by someone else;  (f) the operational and technical requirements necessary for the safe and reliable operation of a carriage service, a telecommunications network or a facility;  (g) the economically efficient operation of a carriage service, a telecommunications network or a facility." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Commission must take the following matters into account in making an access determination:  (a) whether the determination will promote the long-term interests of end-users of carriage services or of services supplied by means of carriage services;  (b) the legitimate business interests of a carrier or carriage service provider who supplies, or is capable of supplying, the declared service, and the carrier’s or provider’s investment in facilities used to supply the declared service;  (c) the interests of all persons who have rights to use the declared service;  (d) the direct costs of providing access to the declared service;  (e) the value to a person of extensions, or enhancement of capability, whose cost is borne by someone else;  (f) the operational and technical requirements necessary for the safe and reliable operation of a carriage service, a telecommunications network or a facility;  (g) the economically efficient operation of a carriage service, a telecommunications network or a facility."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "6e6d40f44e9153e35d22c29f5077f3ebef0243fea85394c2da19ac79e01a76ce" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-118-2 ;
    cof:pageNumber "122"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Commission must consider various factors when making an access determination. Prevents Commission from making access determinations with certain effects." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010.pdf> ;
