    values:originalText "(2) Examples of grounds for believing as mentioned in subparagraph (1)(g)(i) include:  (a) evidence that the access seeker is not creditworthy; and  (b) repeated failures by the access seeker to comply with the terms and conditions on which the same or similar access has been provided (whether or not by the carrier or carriage service provider)." ;
    cof:pageNumber "124"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-120-2-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
