concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-128-2-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "128(2) Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-128-2-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) If a person applies to the Federal Court under subsection 39B(1) of the Judiciary Act 1903 for a writ or injunction in relation to a decision of the Commission to make an access determination, the Court must not make any orders staying or otherwise affecting the operation or implementation of the decision pending the finalisation of the application. Subdivision B—Public inquiries about proposals to make access determinations 152BCH  Access determination to be made after public inquiry" ;
    skos:definition "(2) If a person applies to the Federal Court under subsection 39B(1) of the Judiciary Act 1903 for a writ or injunction in relation to a decision of the Commission to make an access determination, the Court must not make any orders staying or otherwise affecting the operation or implementation of the decision pending the finalisation of the application. Subdivision B—Public inquiries about proposals to make access determinations 152BCH  Access determination to be made after public inquiry"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "e3b239a097d1d72a92da96185c0ef1ccda92612bdbffefabb50a8e12cad3e1a0" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-128-2 ;
    cof:pageNumber "132"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Exempts interim access determination from subsection (1) Commission must hold a public inquiry about access to declared service. Court must not make orders staying or otherwise affecting the operation or implementation of the decision pending finalisation of the application." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
