concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-132-2-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "132(3) Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-132-2-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) The Commission is not required to hold a public inquiry under Part 25 of the Telecommunications Act 1997 about a proposal to revoke an access determination if the Commission is satisfied that each:  (a) carrier or service provider; and  (b) access seeker; whose interests are likely to be affected by the revocation has consented in writing to the revocation." ;
    skos:definition "(3) The Commission is not required to hold a public inquiry under Part 25 of the Telecommunications Act 1997 about a proposal to revoke an access determination if the Commission is satisfied that each:  (a) carrier or service provider; and  (b) access seeker; whose interests are likely to be affected by the revocation has consented in writing to the revocation."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "4a1d5dd00156b06f31a3dfcd9ca488abfb4cbb59753f3240aa25d6b905c4152d" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-132-2 ;
    cof:pageNumber "136"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Commission may extend 6-month period for making final access determination Consent required for revocation of access determination" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
