concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-152bd a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "152BD Binding rules of conduct"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-152bd ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Commission may make written rules that:  (a) specify any or all of the terms and conditions on which a carrier or carriage service provider is to comply with any or all of the standard access obligations applicable to the carrier or provider in relation to a specified declared service; or  (b) require a carrier or carriage service provider to comply with any or all of the standard access obligations applicable to the carrier or provider in relation to a specified declared service in a manner specified in the rules; if the Commission considers that there is an urgent need to do so. Note: For variation and revocation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.  (2) Rules under subsection (1) are to be known as binding rules of conduct.  (3) Binding rules of conduct may be of general application or may be limited as provided in the rules.  (4) In particular, binding rules of conduct may be limited to:  (a) particular carriers or carriage service providers; or  (b) particular classes of carriers or carriage service providers; or ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00891  Schedule 1  Amendments" ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Commission may make written rules that:  (a) specify any or all of the terms and conditions on which a carrier or carriage service provider is to comply with any or all of the standard access obligations applicable to the carrier or provider in relation to a specified declared service; or  (b) require a carrier or carriage service provider to comply with any or all of the standard access obligations applicable to the carrier or provider in relation to a specified declared service in a manner specified in the rules; if the Commission considers that there is an urgent need to do so. Note: For variation and revocation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.  (2) Rules under subsection (1) are to be known as binding rules of conduct.  (3) Binding rules of conduct may be of general application or may be limited as provided in the rules.  (4) In particular, binding rules of conduct may be limited to:  (a) particular carriers or carriage service providers; or  (b) particular classes of carriers or carriage service providers; or ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00891  Schedule 1  Amendments"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "1753f0f1c79b6e7a9ab13cb538dd47c4e1dc6a9427795087815d9a102f4383f7" ;
    cof:pageNumber "141"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-152bd-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-152bd-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-152bd-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-152bd-ss-4 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010.pdf> ;
