doc:sch-1-sec-138-2-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "138(1) Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Commission must take the following matters into account in making binding rules of conduct:  (a) whether the binding rules of conduct will promote the long-term interests of end-users of carriage services or of services supplied by means of carriage services;  (b) the legitimate business interests of a carrier or carriage service provider who supplies, or is capable of supplying, the declared service, and the carrier’s or provider’s investment in facilities used to supply the declared service;  (c) the interests of all persons who have rights to use the declared service;  (d) the direct costs of providing access to the declared service;  (e) the value to a person of extensions, or enhancement of capability, whose cost is borne by someone else;  (f) the operational and technical requirements necessary for the safe and reliable operation of a carriage service, a telecommunications network or a facility;  (g) the economically efficient operation of a carriage service, a telecommunications network or a facility. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00891  Amendments  Schedule 1 Telecommunications access regime  Part 2  Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer Safeguards) Act 2010          139" ;
    cof:pageNumber "142"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-138-2-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "138(2) Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-138-2-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) If a carrier or carriage service provider who supplies, or is capable of supplying, the declared service supplies one or more other eligible services, then, in making binding rules of conduct that are applicable to the carrier or provider, as the case may be, the Commission may take into account:  (a) the characteristics of those other eligible services; and  (b) the costs associated with those other eligible services; and  (c) the revenues associated with those other eligible services; and  (d) the demand for those other eligible services." ;
    skos:definition "(2) If a carrier or carriage service provider who supplies, or is capable of supplying, the declared service supplies one or more other eligible services, then, in making binding rules of conduct that are applicable to the carrier or provider, as the case may be, the Commission may take into account:  (a) the characteristics of those other eligible services; and  (b) the costs associated with those other eligible services; and  (c) the revenues associated with those other eligible services; and  (d) the demand for those other eligible services."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "fe56b17d170448a594bac3e8759402f080da2716de53a935e0df72b5a29dffd1" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-138-2 ;
    cof:pageNumber "142"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Commission may take into account characteristics, costs, revenues, and demand of other eligible services when making binding rules." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010.pdf, p.142" ;
    cml:asserts concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-138-2-ss-2-norm .
