concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-138-2-ss-5 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "138(5) Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-138-2-ss-5 ;
    values:originalText "(5) For the purposes of taking a particular matter into account under this section, the Commission is not required to obtain information, or further information, that is not already in the possession of the Commission if it is not reasonably practicable for the Commission to do so, having regard to the urgent need to make the binding rules of conduct." ;
    skos:definition "(5) For the purposes of taking a particular matter into account under this section, the Commission is not required to obtain information, or further information, that is not already in the possession of the Commission if it is not reasonably practicable for the Commission to do so, having regard to the urgent need to make the binding rules of conduct."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "c589ac602a743628abf0c325b98f0cde9e276f35eabd97ec9a10c39cbb23ed01" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-138-2 ;
    cof:pageNumber "142"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Commission is not required to obtain information if it is not reasonably practicable. Exempts subsection (4) from limitation by subsection 33(3A) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901." ;
