concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-142-2-ss-1 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "142(1) Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-142-2-ss-1 ;
    values:originalText "(1) If the Federal Court is satisfied, on the application of:  (a) an access seeker; or  (b) a carrier; or  (c) a carriage service provider; that a person has engaged, is engaging, or is proposing to engage in conduct that constitutes a contravention of binding rules of conduct, the Court may make any or all of the following orders: ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00891  Schedule 1  Amendments" ;
    skos:definition "(1) If the Federal Court is satisfied, on the application of:  (a) an access seeker; or  (b) a carrier; or  (c) a carriage service provider; that a person has engaged, is engaging, or is proposing to engage in conduct that constitutes a contravention of binding rules of conduct, the Court may make any or all of the following orders: ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00891  Schedule 1  Amendments"@en ;
