concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-148-2-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "148(2) Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-148-2-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) If:  (a) under subsection 152BE(2), an agreement becomes an access agreement after the commencement of this section; and ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00891  Amendments  Schedule 1 Telecommunications access regime  Part 2  Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer Safeguards) Act 2010          149  (b) the agreement was entered into after the commencement of this section; the carrier or carriage service provider who supplies, or proposes to supply, the service to which the agreement relates must, within 28 days after the day on which the agreement became an access agreement, give the Commission:  (c) a copy of the agreement; and  (d) a written statement setting out such information (if any) about the agreement as is specified in an instrument in force under subsection (5)." ;
    skos:definition "(2) If:  (a) under subsection 152BE(2), an agreement becomes an access agreement after the commencement of this section; and ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00891  Amendments  Schedule 1 Telecommunications access regime  Part 2  Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer Safeguards) Act 2010          149  (b) the agreement was entered into after the commencement of this section; the carrier or carriage service provider who supplies, or proposes to supply, the service to which the agreement relates must, within 28 days after the day on which the agreement became an access agreement, give the Commission:  (c) a copy of the agreement; and  (d) a written statement setting out such information (if any) about the agreement as is specified in an instrument in force under subsection (5)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "c1d7815e32640cc25484f7e5e798438e683bdb7ba031fe48b7c3e42393c00026" ;
