concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-166 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "166 After section 152CBA"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-166 ;
    values:originalText "Insert: 152CBAA  Fixed principles terms and conditions  (1) A special access undertaking may provide that a term or condition specified in the undertaking is a fixed principles term or condition for a period that, under the undertaking, is expressed to be the notional fixed period for the fixed principles term or condition.  (2) If the undertaking does so, the undertaking may also provide that one or more specified circumstances are qualifying circumstances in relation to the fixed principles term or condition.  (3) The notional fixed period for a fixed principles term or condition must:  (a) begin when the undertaking comes into operation; and  (b) end:  (i) at the expiry time of the undertaking; or ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00891  Schedule 1  Amendments" ;
    skos:definition "Insert: 152CBAA  Fixed principles terms and conditions  (1) A special access undertaking may provide that a term or condition specified in the undertaking is a fixed principles term or condition for a period that, under the undertaking, is expressed to be the notional fixed period for the fixed principles term or condition.  (2) If the undertaking does so, the undertaking may also provide that one or more specified circumstances are qualifying circumstances in relation to the fixed principles term or condition.  (3) The notional fixed period for a fixed principles term or condition must:  (a) begin when the undertaking comes into operation; and  (b) end:  (i) at the expiry time of the undertaking; or ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00891  Schedule 1  Amendments"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "1a450052ae66599be27975da71a593c77c7b8c36ac1a6b145b1ab00b91355eed" ;
    cof:pageNumber "155"^^xsd:integer ;
