    skos:definition "(4) If:  (a) a fixed principles term or condition is specified in a special access undertaking; and  (b) the undertaking ceases to be in operation before the end of the notional fixed period for the fixed principles term or condition; the fixed principles term or condition ceases to be in operation when the undertaking ceases to be in operation. Note: Even though the fixed principles term or condition ceases to be in operation when the undertaking ceases to be in operation, subsection (5) ensures that a fresh undertaking can include an identical fixed principles term or condition. Consequences—acceptance of other undertaking"@en ;
