concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-219 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "219 Subsections 9(2) and (3)"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-219 ;
    values:originalText "Repeal the subsections, substitute:  (2) The obligation mentioned in paragraph (1)(a) includes the obligation to supply standard telephone services to people in Australia on request.  (2A) The obligation mentioned in paragraph (1)(b) includes the obligation to supply, install and maintain payphones in Australia.  (2B) The obligation mentioned in paragraph (1)(c) includes the obligation to supply prescribed carriage services to people in Australia on request.  (2C) An obligation does not arise under paragraph (1)(a) or subsection (2) in relation to the supply of a standard telephone service to a person on request unless the request complies with the ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00891  Amendments  Schedule 1 Universal service regime  Part 4  Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer Safeguards) Act 2010          177 requirements (if any) set out in a determination under subsection (2D).  (2D) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine requirements for the purposes of subsection (2C).  (2E) An obligation does not arise under paragraph (1)(a) or subsection (2) in relation to the supply of a standard telephone service in the circumstances (if any) specified in a determination under subsection (3).  (3) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine circumstances for the purposes of subsection (2E)." ;
    skos:definition "Repeal the subsections, substitute:  (2) The obligation mentioned in paragraph (1)(a) includes the obligation to supply standard telephone services to people in Australia on request.  (2A) The obligation mentioned in paragraph (1)(b) includes the obligation to supply, install and maintain payphones in Australia.  (2B) The obligation mentioned in paragraph (1)(c) includes the obligation to supply prescribed carriage services to people in Australia on request.  (2C) An obligation does not arise under paragraph (1)(a) or subsection (2) in relation to the supply of a standard telephone service to a person on request unless the request complies with the ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00891  Amendments  Schedule 1 Universal service regime  Part 4  Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer Safeguards) Act 2010          177 requirements (if any) set out in a determination under subsection (2D).  (2D) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine requirements for the purposes of subsection (2C).  (2E) An obligation does not arise under paragraph (1)(a) or subsection (2) in relation to the supply of a standard telephone service in the circumstances (if any) specified in a determination under subsection (3).  (3) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine circumstances for the purposes of subsection (2E)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "45006b563b2fa2182b7ea81cca2aac16faa404d7946d1c0f51f91fbff6cf069d" ;
    cof:pageNumber "180"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-219-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-219-ss-2a ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-219-ss-2b ;
