concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-12ec a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "12EC Performance benchmarks"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-12ec ;
    values:originalText "Determination  (1) The Minister may make a written determination setting out standards to be complied with by a primary universal service provider in relation to any or all of the following matters:  (a) the terms and conditions of the supply of a standard telephone service to a customer, other than price-related terms and conditions;  (b) the reliability of a standard telephone service supplied to a customer;  (c) the supply of a temporary standard telephone service to a customer;  (d) the maximum period within which a primary universal service provider must supply a standard telephone service following the making of a request by a prospective customer;  (e) the maximum period within which a primary universal service provider must rectify a fault or service difficulty relating to a standard telephone service following the making of a report by a customer about the fault or service difficulty; ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00891  Schedule 1  Amendments" ;
    skos:definition "Determination  (1) The Minister may make a written determination setting out standards to be complied with by a primary universal service provider in relation to any or all of the following matters:  (a) the terms and conditions of the supply of a standard telephone service to a customer, other than price-related terms and conditions;  (b) the reliability of a standard telephone service supplied to a customer;  (c) the supply of a temporary standard telephone service to a customer;  (d) the maximum period within which a primary universal service provider must supply a standard telephone service following the making of a request by a prospective customer;  (e) the maximum period within which a primary universal service provider must rectify a fault or service difficulty relating to a standard telephone service following the making of a report by a customer about the fault or service difficulty; ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00891  Schedule 1  Amendments"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "f4e40bad2951c8acf757e8eb5c6244a26cad05075446cde2ef81abaadb4cdca2" ;
    cof:pageNumber "183"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Minister may make written determination setting standards for primary universal service providers." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010.pdf, p.183" ;
    cml:asserts concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-12ec-norm .
