    skos:prefLabel "12EE(1) Performance benchmarks"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-12ee-ss-1 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Minister may make a written determination setting out standards to be complied with by a primary universal service provider in relation to any or all of the following matters:  (a) the characteristics of a payphone carriage service;  (b) the supply, installation or maintenance of a payphone;  (c) the supply of a payphone carriage service;  (d) the reliability of a payphone;  (e) the reliability of a payphone carriage service; ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00891  Amendments  Schedule 1 Universal service regime  Part 4  Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer Safeguards) Act 2010          183  (f) the maximum period within which a primary universal service provider must rectify a fault or service difficulty relating to a payphone following the making of a report about a fault or service difficulty;  (g) the maximum period within which a primary universal service provider must rectify a fault or service difficulty relating to a payphone carriage service following the making of a report about a fault or service difficulty;  (h) the handling of requests for the removal of a payphone;  (i) any other matter concerning:  (i) the supply, installation or maintenance of a payphone; or  (ii) the supply of a payphone carriage service." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Minister may make a written determination setting out standards to be complied with by a primary universal service provider in relation to any or all of the following matters:  (a) the characteristics of a payphone carriage service;  (b) the supply, installation or maintenance of a payphone;  (c) the supply of a payphone carriage service;  (d) the reliability of a payphone;  (e) the reliability of a payphone carriage service; ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00891  Amendments  Schedule 1 Universal service regime  Part 4  Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer Safeguards) Act 2010          183  (f) the maximum period within which a primary universal service provider must rectify a fault or service difficulty relating to a payphone following the making of a report about a fault or service difficulty;  (g) the maximum period within which a primary universal service provider must rectify a fault or service difficulty relating to a payphone carriage service following the making of a report about a fault or service difficulty;  (h) the handling of requests for the removal of a payphone;  (i) any other matter concerning:  (i) the supply, installation or maintenance of a payphone; or  (ii) the supply of a payphone carriage service."@en ;
