concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-184-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "184 Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-184-2 ;
    values:originalText "Consumer Safeguards) Act 2010  (8) Subsection (7) does not, by implication, limit subsection 33(3A) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901. Provider must meet or exceed minimum benchmarks  (9) A primary universal service provider must meet or exceed a minimum benchmark set by an instrument under subsection (6). Clause 1 of Schedule 1 to the Telecommunications Act 1997 does not apply to a breach of a standard  (10) Clause 1 of Schedule 1 to the Telecommunications Act 1997 does not apply to a contravention of a standard in force under subsection (1). Note: Clause 1 of Schedule 1 to the Telecommunications Act 1997 requires carriers to comply with this Act. Clause 1 of Schedule 2 to the Telecommunications Act 1997 does not apply to a breach of a standard  (11) Clause 1 of Schedule 2 to the Telecommunications Act 1997 does not apply to a contravention of a standard in force under subsection (1). Note: Clause 1 of Schedule 2 to the Telecommunications Act 1997 requires carriage service providers to comply with this Act." ;
    skos:definition "Consumer Safeguards) Act 2010  (8) Subsection (7) does not, by implication, limit subsection 33(3A) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901. Provider must meet or exceed minimum benchmarks  (9) A primary universal service provider must meet or exceed a minimum benchmark set by an instrument under subsection (6). Clause 1 of Schedule 1 to the Telecommunications Act 1997 does not apply to a breach of a standard  (10) Clause 1 of Schedule 1 to the Telecommunications Act 1997 does not apply to a contravention of a standard in force under subsection (1). Note: Clause 1 of Schedule 1 to the Telecommunications Act 1997 requires carriers to comply with this Act. Clause 1 of Schedule 2 to the Telecommunications Act 1997 does not apply to a breach of a standard  (11) Clause 1 of Schedule 2 to the Telecommunications Act 1997 does not apply to a contravention of a standard in force under subsection (1). Note: Clause 1 of Schedule 2 to the Telecommunications Act 1997 requires carriage service providers to comply with this Act."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "6dc73eabdd8a6fb43f22537c8088fb7dba9c468f96e0808bf567aa75882e435d" ;
    cof:pageNumber "188"^^xsd:integer ;
