concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-12ef a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "12EF Rules about the location of payphones"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-12ef ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Minister may make a determination setting out rules to be complied with by a primary universal service provider in relation to the places or areas in which payphones are to be located. Compliance  (2) A primary universal service provider must comply with a determination under subsection (1).  (3) If a primary universal service provider complies with a determination under subsection (1), the provider is taken to have complied with an obligation under paragraph 9(1)(b) or subsection 9(2A), to the extent to which the obligation relates to the location of payphones. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00891  Amendments  Schedule 1 Universal service regime  Part 4  Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer Safeguards) Act 2010          185 Determination prevails over inconsistent instruments  (4) Each of the following instruments:  (a) an approved policy statement for a primary universal service provider;  (b) an approved standard marketing plan for a primary universal service provider; has no effect to the extent to which the instrument is inconsistent with a determination in force under subsection (1). Determination is a legislative instrument  (5) A determination under subsection (1) is a legislative instrument." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Minister may make a determination setting out rules to be complied with by a primary universal service provider in relation to the places or areas in which payphones are to be located. Compliance  (2) A primary universal service provider must comply with a determination under subsection (1).  (3) If a primary universal service provider complies with a determination under subsection (1), the provider is taken to have complied with an obligation under paragraph 9(1)(b) or subsection 9(2A), to the extent to which the obligation relates to the location of payphones. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00891  Amendments  Schedule 1 Universal service regime  Part 4  Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer Safeguards) Act 2010          185 Determination prevails over inconsistent instruments  (4) Each of the following instruments:  (a) an approved policy statement for a primary universal service provider;  (b) an approved standard marketing plan for a primary universal service provider; has no effect to the extent to which the instrument is inconsistent with a determination in force under subsection (1). Determination is a legislative instrument  (5) A determination under subsection (1) is a legislative instrument."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "b351bd17de24474339c7082f85e1b42d620c2a66b687a17e1acabb2295615c2e" ;
    cof:pageNumber "188"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-12ef-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-12ef-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-12ef-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-12ef-ss-4 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-12ef-ss-5 ;
