concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-117e a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "117E Performance benchmarks"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-117e ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, set minimum benchmarks in relation to compliance by carriage service providers with a standard in force under section 117D.  (2) An instrument under this section may be of general application or may be limited as provided in the instrument.  (3) Subsection (2) does not, by implication, limit subsection 33(3A) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, set minimum benchmarks in relation to compliance by carriage service providers with a standard in force under section 117D.  (2) An instrument under this section may be of general application or may be limited as provided in the instrument.  (3) Subsection (2) does not, by implication, limit subsection 33(3A) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901."@en ;
