concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-572f a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "572F Matters to be included in an infringement notice"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-572f ;
    values:originalText "(1) An infringement notice must:  (a) set out the name of the person to whom the notice is given; and  (b) set out the name of the authorised infringement notice officer who gave the notice; and  (c) set out brief details of the alleged contravention; and  (d) contain a statement to the effect that the matter will not be dealt with by the Federal Court if the penalty specified in the notice is paid to the ACMA, on behalf of the Commonwealth, within:  (i) 28 days after the notice is given; or  (ii) if the ACMA allows a longer period—that longer period; and  (e) give an explanation of how payment of the penalty is to be made; and ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00891  Amendments  Schedule 1 Infringement notices etc.  Part 7  Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer Safeguards) Act 2010          205  (f) set out such other matters (if any) as are specified by the regulations. Note: For the amount of penalty, see section 572G.  (2) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(c), the brief details must include the following information in relation to the alleged contravention:  (a) the date of the alleged contravention;  (b) the civil penalty provision that was allegedly contravened." ;
    skos:definition "(1) An infringement notice must:  (a) set out the name of the person to whom the notice is given; and  (b) set out the name of the authorised infringement notice officer who gave the notice; and  (c) set out brief details of the alleged contravention; and  (d) contain a statement to the effect that the matter will not be dealt with by the Federal Court if the penalty specified in the notice is paid to the ACMA, on behalf of the Commonwealth, within:  (i) 28 days after the notice is given; or  (ii) if the ACMA allows a longer period—that longer period; and  (e) give an explanation of how payment of the penalty is to be made; and ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00891  Amendments  Schedule 1 Infringement notices etc.  Part 7  Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer Safeguards) Act 2010          205  (f) set out such other matters (if any) as are specified by the regulations. Note: For the amount of penalty, see section 572G.  (2) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(c), the brief details must include the following information in relation to the alleged contravention:  (a) the date of the alleged contravention;  (b) the civil penalty provision that was allegedly contravened."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "158dfb3483a15bfbeabd859b4dda07ecc00a3d2e8ddb3d1640a16b22addd6fd2" ;
    cof:pageNumber "208"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-572f-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-572f-ss-2 ;
