concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-251 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "251 Section 7 (definition of civil penalty provision)"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-251 ;
    values:originalText "Repeal the definition, substitute: civil penalty provision means:  (a) a provision of this Act that is declared by this Act to be a civil penalty provision; or  (b) a provision of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999 that is declared by that Act to be a civil penalty provision. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00891  Schedule 1  Amendments" ;
    skos:definition "Repeal the definition, substitute: civil penalty provision means:  (a) a provision of this Act that is declared by this Act to be a civil penalty provision; or  (b) a provision of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999 that is declared by that Act to be a civil penalty provision. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00891  Schedule 1  Amendments"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "b674651b5b3d382e02d4fa2c48d45bc37336a1611397b3a83afd462d6a54699e" ;
