concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-safeguards-act-2010-sch-1-sec-125aa a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "125AA ACMA must determine an industry standard if directed by"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-125aa ;
    values:originalText "the Minister  (1) The ACMA may, by legislative instrument, determine a standard that:  (a) applies to participants in a particular section of the telecommunications industry; and  (b) deals with one or more matters relating to the telecommunications activities of those participants. Note 1: For examples of matters that may be dealt with by industry standards, see section 113. Note 2: For variation and revocation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.  (2) A standard under subsection (1) is to be known as an industry standard.  (3) If the ACMA is satisfied that a body or association represents that section of the telecommunications industry, the ACMA must consult the body or association before determining a standard under subsection (1).  (4) The Minister may, in writing, direct the ACMA to determine a standard under subsection (1) that:  (a) applies to participants in a specified section of the telecommunications industry; and  (b) deals with one or more specified matters relating to the telecommunications activities of those participants. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00891  Amendments  Schedule 1 Industry standards  Part 9  Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer Safeguards) Act 2010          211  (5) The ACMA must not determine a standard under subsection (1) unless it does so in accordance with a direction under subsection (4). ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00891  ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00891   Notes to the  Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer Safeguards) Act 2010  Table of Acts  Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer Safeguards) Act 2010                    213 Notes to the Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer Safeguards) Act 2010 Note 1 The Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer 2010 amended as indicated in the Tables below. Table of Acts Act Number and year Date of Assent Date of commencement Application, saving or transitional provisions Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer Safeguards) Act 2010 140, 2010" ;
    skos:definition "the Minister  (1) The ACMA may, by legislative instrument, determine a standard that:  (a) applies to participants in a particular section of the telecommunications industry; and  (b) deals with one or more matters relating to the telecommunications activities of those participants. Note 1: For examples of matters that may be dealt with by industry standards, see section 113. Note 2: For variation and revocation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.  (2) A standard under subsection (1) is to be known as an industry standard.  (3) If the ACMA is satisfied that a body or association represents that section of the telecommunications industry, the ACMA must consult the body or association before determining a standard under subsection (1).  (4) The Minister may, in writing, direct the ACMA to determine a standard under subsection (1) that:  (a) applies to participants in a specified section of the telecommunications industry; and  (b) deals with one or more specified matters relating to the telecommunications activities of those participants. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00891  Amendments  Schedule 1 Industry standards  Part 9  Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer Safeguards) Act 2010          211  (5) The ACMA must not determine a standard under subsection (1) unless it does so in accordance with a direction under subsection (4). ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00891  ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012C00891   Notes to the  Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer Safeguards) Act 2010  Table of Acts  Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer Safeguards) Act 2010                    213 Notes to the Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer Safeguards) Act 2010 Note 1 The Telecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and Consumer 2010 amended as indicated in the Tables below. Table of Acts Act Number and year Date of Assent Date of commencem"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "e115b5c94ba427ff5d8c6333a58aad5e160e1c74042b853cbb605fae46e27b37" ;
    cof:pageNumber "214"^^xsd:integer ;
